# Hidden input shared propagates beta -> gamma, but the root caller and
# eligible lexical parents supply no binding. beta's later own declaration
# does not make a preceding read visible or provide a future type seed.
# Keep this original program as a refusal, never a silent null/default or
# another method's field. Without a type source, diagnose the original free use.
fn: beta () int
    c.printf: "beta sees shared=%d\n" shared
    int: shared 222
    return: 0
end: beta

fn: gamma () int
    beta()
    return: 0
end: gamma

gamma()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
